## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

The normalized v1 manifest now rejects multiple exact revisions of one
dependency identity and rejects dependency identities that are also declared as
conflicts or superseded packages. External contract tests cover each
contradictory relationship shape.

Deterministic content revisions now reuse the same canonical member validation
as package manifests and member construction, including the reserved manifest
path, portable identity, byte limits, digest shape, media type, and role.

The content-revision digest also length-prefixes every variable-width member
metadata field that participates in the hash, with regression coverage proving
that different media-type/role boundaries cannot produce one revision.
